      transliteration: "Kaṭal vaṇṇaṉ tiruvaṭi\nkāṭṭiṭṭu uyvittāy\nmaṭa mayil mēl koṇṭa\nmāyavaṉ taṉṉai\nkoṭai uṭai vēntaṉ eṉṟu\nkūṟum eṉṉōṭu\nkaṭal vaṇṇaṉ kamala pātam\nkāṭṭi vāḻvittāy.",
      english: "You showed the sacred feet of the ocean-dark one\nand caused me to be liberated.\nThe wondrous one who rides on the young peacock —\nyou told me, along with me:\n'He is the generous king' —\nand showing the lotus feet of the ocean-dark one,\nyou gave me life.",
      tamilUrai: "கடல் வண்ணன் திருவடி காட்டிட்டு உய்வித்தாய். மட மயில் மேல் கொண்ட மாயவன் — கொடையுடை வேந்தன் என்று என்னோடு கூறி, கடல் வண்ணன் கமல பாதம் காட்டி வாழ்வித்தாய்.",
      altTranslation: "You showed the sacred feet of the ocean-dark one and liberated me.\nThe wondrous one who rides the young peacock —\nyou told me, along with me: 'He is the generous king' —\nand showing the ocean-dark one's lotus feet, you gave me life.",
      theme: "Liberation and Life Through the Teacher — vāḻvittāy (you gave life) and uyvittāy (you liberated/saved) are synonyms that together declare the full scope of the ācārya's gift.",
      note: "Vāḻvittāy — 'you caused to live, you enlivened' — adds a physical dimension to the spiritual salvation already described. The teacher's showing of the Lord's feet is both liberating (uyvu) and life-giving (vāḻvu) — two registers of the same transforming act."
