      transliteration: "Kaṭal vaṇṇaṉ aruḷ\nkaṇṇārak kāṭṭiṉāy\nmaṭa mayil kōlam koṇṭa\nmāyavaṉ taṉṉai\nkoṭai uṭai vēntaṉ eṉṟu\nkūṟum eṉṉōṭu\nkaṭal vaṇṇaṉ kamala pātam\nkaṇṭu uyntēṉē.",
      english: "You showed the grace of the ocean-dark one\nto the full of my eyes.\nThe wondrous one who has taken the peacock's beauty as his own —\nyou told me, along with me:\n'He is the generous king' —\nand I, having seen the lotus feet\nof the ocean-dark one, was saved.",
      tamilUrai: "கடல் வண்ணன் அருள் கண்ணாரக் காட்டினாய். மட மயில் கோலம் கொண்ட மாயவன் — கொடையுடை வேந்தன் என்று என்னோடு கூறி, கடல் வண்ணன் கமல பாதம் கண்டு உய்ந்தேன்.",
      altTranslation: "You showed the grace of the ocean-dark one to the full of my eyes.\nThe wondrous one who has taken on the peacock's beauty —\nyou told me, along with me: 'He is the generous king' —\nand seeing the ocean-dark one's lotus feet, I was saved.",
      theme: "Grace Made Visible — the teacher shows not just the Lord's feet but his grace (aruḷ); what is transmitted is divine grace itself, made visible.",
      note: "Aruḷ (grace, compassion) as the object of the showing marks a theological refinement: the teacher does not merely show the Lord's form but his grace — his disposition of compassion toward the devotee. Vision of grace is deeper than vision of form."
